# Architecture Rules

`AGENTS.md` and `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` are the source of truth. Check both before architectural changes.

## Required

* Keep the backend serverless in a single TypeScript pnpm monorepo.
* API Gateway HTTP API + Lambda; S3 docs; SQS ingestion; DynamoDB metadata/sessions/usage; embeddings/LLM via `EmbeddingProvider` / `LLMProvider` (interim Voyage + Gemini; target Bedrock); Qdrant via `VectorStore`.
* Thin handlers in `services/*`; logic in `packages/core`; AWS/provider SDKs only in `packages/providers`.

## Cost (hard budget)

Near-zero portfolio stack; **worst case ≤ $10/month**. Be stringent on every resource and config.

* No always-on compute; no EC2/ECS/EKS/RDS/Redis/Kafka/OpenSearch/NAT “for convenience.”
* Lambda: low memory (start 128–256 MB), short timeouts, no provisioned concurrency.
* DynamoDB on-demand only; no DAX/global tables/extra GSIs.
* S3 private + lifecycle; SQS small payloads; HTTP API not REST API.
* CloudWatch short retention; no chatty custom metrics or document body logs.
* Embeddings/LLM: prefer Voyage + Gemini free/low tiers at portfolio volume; when on Bedrock, smallest suitable models. Hard token/top-K/quota caps; abstain over expensive retries.
* Before adding/raising capacity, state monthly cost impact and stay inside budget.

## Coding / AWS SDK

* Style: modular, reusable, simple, straightforward; no bloat or redundant copies (see `coding-style.mdc` / `AGENTS.md`).
* AWS SDK v3 modular clients only; reuse clients outside the handler; least-privilege IAM.
* Small esbuild bundles; bounded retries/timeouts; validate at boundaries; no hard-coded secrets/regions/model IDs.
* Prefer presigned S3 uploads and idempotent writes.

## Multi-Tenancy / RAG / Ingestion / Security

* Never trust client `tenantId`; derive from Cognito JWT `sub`; tenant-filter every search/lookup.
* Retrieve → confidence gate → generate with citations; abstain if weak; treat docs as untrusted.
* Async idempotent ingestion with deterministic IDs, upserts, status, SQS retries/DLQ.
* No secrets in git/frontend; short-lived presigned URLs; validate uploads; scan for secrets before commit/push.

## Scope Control

Do not add infrastructure for theoretical scale. If a change conflicts with these rules, update architecture docs first.
